    "mechanism_family": "structure_confirmed_donchian_trend_breakout",
    "market_inefficiency": "A classic Donchian20 break only becomes tradeable mid-frequency continuation when three structural filters co-occur: (1) the break bar closes beyond prev_high20/prev_low20 with dual volume acceptance (vol_z20 climax + vol_ma20_ratio expansion), (2) a 2-bar rising/falling structure proves trend initiation rather than a one-tick spike, and (3) H1 slope has non-trivial magnitude so the cascade has directional drift. Mild-volume flat-slope breaks are the prior L1 payoff attractor and are explicitly excluded. An ATR regime band rejects both dead chop and chaotic spike regimes.",
    "counterparty_source": "Range-bound and breakout-fade accounts with stops parked beyond the 20-bar Donchian extreme; under volume-accepted structural breaks their forced covering supplies one-sided flow that HTF slope prolongs.",
    "why_edge_exists": "Stop placement beyond recent extremes is inventory management, not instant fair-value arb. Requiring structure (2-bar momentum into break) + slope magnitude + dual volume + ATR band filters the low-payoff fake breaks that killed vol_accepted_donchian_h1_continuation. Edge is harvested with partial_tp_atr scale-out then atr_trailing (no fixed % TP) so winners clear L1/Gate2 payoff floors after friction.",
    "edge_decay_conditions": "Breakouts overcrowded with fade liquidity; vol_z or vol_ma20_ratio collapse; H1 slope magnitude flattens/flips; ATR exits the mid-regime band into chop or panic; continuation cannot cover 20x+fees (payoff attractor ≤1.2).",
    "required_market_regime": "Directional or transitioning mid-frequency markets with ATR in a tradable band and volume expansion on Donchian breaks — not deep chop, not one-bar noise spikes, not mild-volume flat-slope Donchian noise.",
    "entry_logic": "LONG ALL: (1) close cross_above prev_high20; (2) close > close[offset=1] AND close[offset=1] > close[offset=2] (2-bar rising structure); (3) h1_slope4 > 0.0015 (meaningful HTF thrust); (4) vol_z20 > 1.6; (5) vol_ma20_ratio > 1.2; (6) atr14 > close*0.0025 AND atr14 < close*0.01 (ATR regime / chop filter); (7) close > open. SHORT mirror: cross_below prev_low20, 2-bar falling structure, h1_slope4 < -0.0015, same volume/ATR band, close < open.",
    "exit_logic": "Scale-out partial_tp_atr n_atr=2.5 partial_tp_ratio=0.5 then atr_trailing n_atr=3.5 ATR_14 (role=take_profit). swing_extreme lookback=20 invalidation. Protective SL 0.9% immutable. max_hold_bars=40. No fixed % TP.",
